# Everything in this repository ends up inside a Linux container, so everything
# checks out with LF — on Windows too.
#
# This is not a tidiness preference. Git on Windows converts to CRLF on
# checkout by default, and a shell script with CRLF has "\r" as part of its
# shebang line. The kernel then looks for an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r",
# does not find it, and reports:
#
#     exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint: no such file or directory
#
# which names the script, not the interpreter, and so reads as a missing file.
# Without this file, cloning on Windows produced an image that could not start.
# It went unnoticed because the machine it was developed on had LF in its
# working tree already; only a fresh clone showed it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git must not touch them at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gguf binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.m4a binary
